      "id": 1242816,
      "npm_advisory_id": null,
      "overview": "## Impact\n\nA memory-related vulnerability has been discovered in an upstream library used for Image Optimization can lead to possible remote code execution (RCE) when Next.js runs on glibc-based Linux.\n\n## Workaround\n\nEnsure the version of `sharp` used by Next.js is greater than or equal to `0.35.5`. Fresh installs automatically get a fixed version of `sharp`.\nUpgrading Next.js to the patched versions will ensure package managers automatically provide a fixed version of `sharp` to Next.js.",
      "reported_by": null,
      "title": "Next.js: Unauthenticated Remote Code Execution in Image Optimization API when SVG files are used",
      "metadata": null,
      "cves": [],
